# /etc/boss/deploy.env — per-machine deploy configuration.
#
# Copied here by hand, NOT by the deploy: these values describe the box,
# so a deploy that wrote them would be asserting something it cannot
# know. Sourced by infra/deploy-services.sh with `set -a`, so plain
# KEY=value lines are exported.
#
# BOSS_JOBS_URL — the jobs API that owns this machine's packets, i.e.
# the SYSTEM OF RECORD. It reaches the timer drop-ins the deploy writes
# and this script's own bookkeeping call, and both helpers
# (boss-maintenance-wrap.sh, boss-step.sh) now REFUSE rather than
# default, so an unset value fails loudly instead of filing packets
# somewhere plausible.
#
#   boss-gcp  -> the cluster, which is authoritative:
#                  BOSS_JOBS_URL=http://10.20.0.34:7900
#   cluster   -> itself; leave unset and the local default holds.
#
# The estate model records which is which:
# service_instances.authoritative is true for boss-cluster and false
# for boss-gcp-local.
BOSS_JOBS_URL=http://10.20.0.34:7900
